    <entry xml:lang="en">
        <title>Superimposed Effects of Brill Waves and Scalar Fields in Axisymmetric Critical Collapse</title>
        <published>2026-04-07T00:00:00+00:00</published>
        <updated>2026-04-07T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
        
        <author>
          <name>
            
              Unknown
            
          </name>
        </author>
        
        <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://sylviamesicek.github.io/presentations/urs2026/"/>
        <id>https://sylviamesicek.github.io/presentations/urs2026/</id>
        
        <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;Culmination of my undergraduate work with Dr. John Belz, during which I built a derived a strongly hyperbolic formulation of the Einstien field equations in axisymmetry and implemented a robust, adaptive, finite difference solver for simulating scalar fields and Brill waves.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;</summary>
        
    </entry>
